# Git LFS tracking
#
# IMPORTANT — GitHub Pages compatibility:
# GitHub Pages serves files directly from the git tree. Files tracked with LFS
# are replaced by tiny pointer files in the tree, so GitHub Pages would serve
# the pointer text instead of the actual content. This means any file under
# docs/ that is served to users (images, JSON analytics, leaderboard CSVs,
# plot PNGs/HTMLs) must NOT use LFS — they must remain as regular git objects.
#
# LFS is appropriate for large binary files that are NOT served by GitHub Pages,
# for example private exports, archives, or build artifacts stored outside docs/.

# Private/internal large files (not served via GitHub Pages)
plots/private/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
plots/private/**/*.html filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
